        "top_source": "10.77.0.44",
        "top_source_failures": 16
      },
      "notes": "successful_logins counts both accepted logins in the file (10.77.0.10 publickey at 07:58:11 and 10.77.0.44 password at 08:01:31); the second is the one that matters, which is why the parser emits per-event observations as well."
    },
    {
      "id": "OBS-HTTP-SUMMARY-01",
      "kind": "http_summary",
      "assertion": "approximate",
      "fixture": "tests/fixtures/logs/nginx_access.log",
      "value": {
        "target": "lab-web-01",
        "total_requests": 18,
        "suspicious_requests": 12,
        "suspicious_paths_include": ["/../../etc/passwd", "/api/v1/users", "/.env", "/.git/config", "/phpmyadmin/", "/server-status"]
      },
      "notes": "total_requests is exact. suspicious_requests depends on the parser's declared definition of 'suspicious'; the paths listed are the ones any defensible definition must include, so the path list is the load-bearing part."
    },
    {
      "id": "OBS-HTTP-EVENT-TRAVERSAL",
      "kind": "http_event",
      "assertion": "exact",
      "fixture": "tests/fixtures/logs/nginx_access.log",
